ry from this request is retrieved and applicable, apply its procedure to an actual remaining research action; print compact diagnostics identifying the request/job, entry and commit, what action you took, and the observed result. Treat an applied zero-edit proposal as a legitimate completed decline and report it accurately in diagnostics. If the job is still planning, no new entry was retrieved, or a retrieved entry does not apply to remaining work, report that actual state and continue or finish the research normally. Do not sleep, poll, repeatedly search the harness for an entry, resubmit refinement, or manufacture extra work to wait for a lesson. Finishing the requested research never depends on a refinement edit or a reuse demonstration. Do not count a finalizer-only edit or a completed decline as same-run lesson reuse. Keep diagnostic notes in REPL output and return only the requested cited table in the final answer.",
